WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.668
Step 1. Open the Medicine Administration sub-tab.

1.2
00:00:03.668 --> 00:00:08.900
The chart shows which doses staff recorded for each medicine, at what time,

1.3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.865
and with what status.

2.1
00:00:10.865 --> 00:00:14.526
Step 2. Choose medicines or nutritional products.

2.2
00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:17.171
Care opens the sub-tab on Medications.

2.3
00:00:17.171 --> 00:00:22.892
Select Nutrition to see nutritional products; that view works the same way.

3.1
00:00:22.892 --> 00:00:24.746
Step 3. Read the grid.

3.2
00:00:24.746 --> 00:00:29.706
Each row is one medicine, and four columns show six-hour time slots.

3.3
00:00:29.706 --> 00:00:35.822
A medicine prescribed more than once is grouped; expand it to see each entry.

4.1
00:00:35.822 --> 00:00:41.424
Step 4. Read the doses. Each recorded dose is a button with its time.

4.2
00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:47.431
Green is Completed, yellow is In Progress, and red is any other status.

5.1
00:00:47.431 --> 00:00:53.479
Step 5. Move to other time slots. Select the left arrow to move back one time slot,

5.2
00:00:53.479 --> 00:00:57.602
and the right arrow to move forward one time slot.

6.1
00:00:57.602 --> 00:01:03.060
Step 6. Search for a medicine. Enter the name in the Search Medication box.

6.2
00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:07.657
Care shows only the medicines whose name contains the text.

7.1
00:01:07.657 --> 00:01:13.802
Step 7. Show discontinued medicines. Care hides a medicine that has no active entry.

7.2
00:01:13.802 --> 00:01:19.777
Select Show discontinued to add it to the grid; Care strikes through its name.

8.1
00:01:19.777 --> 00:01:22.120
Step 8. Open the drug chart.

8.2
00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:27.298
To open the printable drug chart, select View Drug Chart.
